1
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,900
Do you know what I do
to backstabbing dogs?

2
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:23,170
I found the person you're looking for.
The other day at the beach,

3
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,340
under the full moon.

4
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,700
They helped someone out of the sea.

5
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,300
Was it you who killed Toone,
you animal?

6
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:37,740
Don't.

7
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,980
You disappeared with the new shirt.

8
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:43,540
What have you been up to?

9
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:47,740
- You gave the order, didn't you?
- I didn't order it.

10
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,100
I did it myself.

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,380
You fuck!

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,100
You really dare to shoot me?

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,860
Remember this.
If I order you to live, you live!

14
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:04,260
If I order you to die, you die!

15
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:06,740
You owe me for life, Singh!

16
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:08,780
Remember that.

17
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:11,320
I already paid you 30 million, boss.

18
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:13,820
You don't need to give it to me.

19
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:16,980
Nop.

20
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:20,740
Listen to him. Don't go against his wish.

21
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,820
Boss just wants you to
distribute the money, that's all.

22
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,060
I said don't give it to me.

23
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,140
I'm giving it to pay the canvassers.

24
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:29,980
I'm running this time.

25
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,740
Who said you're running? I'm running.

26
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,500
What do you want from me, boss?

27
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,410
Whenever you have a problem,
I clear it for you.

28
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,620
When you risked going to jail,
I served the time for you.

29
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:40,780
I'm asking for this.

30
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,290
They're about to announce it soon.

31
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:44,700
Start preparing our campaign.

32
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:45,580
Yes, boss.

33
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:48,620
- Nop, listen to boss.
- Don't interfere!

34
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,100
If you want to run,
go ahead and do it.

35
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,980
But remember my words.

36
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:55,500
We're done! I'm running!

37
00:02:57,660 --> 00:02:58,700
I'm heading out, boss.

38
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:13,820
I'll handle it for you, sir.

39
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:16,260
Keep it quiet.

40
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,580
Understood.

41
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,060
You focus on
your election campaign, sir.

42
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:22,900
Yes.

43
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,740
What's wrong?
You've looked stressed for a while.

44
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:01,820
Why is it so hard to be
a good person, Mom?

45
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:22,110
Being wicked... that's what's easy.

46
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,980
That's why there are
so many of them.

47
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,020
Being a good person requires
strength in your goodness.

48
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,430
So that the people around us
can afford to be good too.

49
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:33,950
Or do you want to live
surrounded by wicked people?

50
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:38,590
Do good, and good will come to you.

51
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,560
It's good to do good, son.

52
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:48,580
Mom.

53
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:53,140
Is Dad a good person?

54
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,300
Why do you ask that?

55
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:05,300
Your father, he was a good man.

56
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,760
What he did, he did to take care of us.

57
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,140
He did it for us.

58
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:15,420
Believe me.

59
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:27,900
Are you hungry?

60
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:29,820
What should we eat?

61
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:30,700
Hmm?

62
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,220
Kaprao, Mom.

63
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:39,140
Okay.

64
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,580
I'll make it for you.

65
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:48,180
So, who's the target
for the hit, boss?

66
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,700
That bastard Rachin.

67
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:52,580
That animal thinks
he's big time now.

68
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,860
He's so fucking old.

69
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:58,220
He's been the only MP forever.
Won't he let anyone else run?

70
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:03,320
- When, boss?
- Right now!

71
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,680
Are you waiting for him
to blow my brains out first?

72
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,900
- Who let you in?
- Someone sent a package for you, sir.

73
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:25,340
What is this? Slimy and disgusting.

74
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:39,860
Ting, go check it out.

75
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:42,660
Find out which hitman Rachin uses.

76
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,020
I think he's settling scores with me.

77
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,140
Yes, boss.

78
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:53,780
Boss.

79
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:54,940
Boss.

80
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:57,540
Hey, Nop!

81
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,500
Nop!

82
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:07,660
Nop!

83
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,060
Boss!

84
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,180
Nop!

85
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:14,660
Nop!

86
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:33,940
Have you ever sat on
a pier like this before?

87
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,300
Do you remember anything?

88
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:38,620
Yes, I have.

89
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,140
I remember that I have.

90
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:45,380
Who brought you? Who were you with?
Do you remember?

91
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,220
I don't remember.

92
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:53,060
It's okay. Just asking in case
you remember something.

93
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,840
How about you come work
at the shop with us?

94
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,180
Listening to Auntie nag is fun.

95
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:00,830
Hmm, Foon.

96
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,060
You don't get to talk.

97
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,420
You're always disappearing,
here and there.

98
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:07,220
It's only because you guys hang out
here that I get to see your faces.

99
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:09,980
Go see what the customer wants.
Go on.

100
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:11,700
Okay!

101
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:15,060
- Walk a little faster!
- Okay!

102
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:16,450
Have a seat.

103
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:18,850
Here, sit, sit. Please, sit.

104
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:25,100
Nam.

105
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:25,900
Hmm?

106
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,700
Have you ever ridden a jet ski?

107
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,020
Yes, I have.

108
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:55,180
Oh, Nam.

109
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:56,260
Come on.

110
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,380
<i>His entire family...</i>

111
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,750
<i>- ...they can't even trace it back...
- ...killed with black magic...</i>

112
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,580
<i>...earth, water, wind, water...</i>

113
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:17,860
I assume you've never seen
this object before.

114
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,060
How do you know I haven't seen it?

115
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,980
Or that you've never even owned it.

116
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:28,860
Unlikely.

117
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:31,620
This object is priceless.

118
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:34,840
It's rare for someone
to possess and own it.

119
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,100
Look, I'm serious.

120
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:41,300
I myself am reluctant to give it up.
Once you own it for a long time,

121
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,980
you feel an indescribable happiness.

122
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,380
You also know about
this ancient book.

123
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,300
I sent people to get it
from the governor of Nan.

124
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,670
But he wouldn't sell.

125
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:54,540
He wouldn't sell,
so I make him disappear.

126
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,540
Hmm, "make him disappear"?
Just him alone?

127
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:02,340
His entire family.
And they can't even trace it back to me.

128
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:05,900
Oh.

129
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,460
Killed with black magic.

130
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,340
My people are quite capable.

131
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:15,580
Then we agree on a price
of one hundred million.

132
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,300
We agreed on fifty, didn't we?

133
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:20,660
That was then.

134
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,540
But now,

135
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:24,860
one hundred million.

136
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,140
The governor of Nan

137
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:31,690
told me this Satra Sutra book
is an ancient artifact,

138
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:34,600
passed down since
before the Rattanakosin era,

139
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:35,580
made from human skin.

140
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,660
The skin of someone with powerful magic.

141
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:41,260
This Satra Sutra book...

142
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:44,660
whoever possesses it
will become superhuman.

143
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,380
Immortal in spirit.

144
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,700
But to open it,

145
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:54,100
you need the blood of someone born
on the 9th day of the 9th month.

146
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:56,940
And you also need the elements:
Earth, Water, Wind, Fire.

147
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:03,660
- Who could have that?
- The original price is fine.

148
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:06,180
Then we agree on
four hundred million.

149
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:09,100
If you don't want it, just go home.

150
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,180
I'm not desperate for
money or anything.

151
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:15,540
Disgusting humans like you
really are despicable.

152
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,620
More vile than wild beasts.

153
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:20,260
Animals eat,

154
00:11:20,330 --> 00:11:21,980
they get full, and they stop.

155
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,660
But people like you are greedy.

156
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,740
You know no end.

157
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,620
You, for instance...

158
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:32,900
must be taught obedience.

159
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:35,260
To worship and to beg.

160
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:38,260
Do you want so?

161
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:40,700
Bow to me and I will let you go.

162
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,860
This is why it's so expensive.

163
00:11:49,650 --> 00:11:52,380
Because I have to hire private bodyguards.

164
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:55,780
Why wouldn't I know?

165
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,780
This book belongs to someone
with magical power.

166
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,980
So I had to hire someon
with magical power to guard it.

167
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:05,980
So is this how you want to go?

168
00:12:09,180 --> 00:12:10,620
If we don't have a deal, then leave.

169
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,060
Nam...

170
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:21,820
Nam...

171
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,700
Wait, Nam! Ouch!

172
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,060
Nam! It's me, Singh!

173
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,860
Nam!

174
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:29,340
Nam, calm down first.

175
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:30,980
Easy now.

176
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,100
It's me.

177
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:34,980
Calm down.

178
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:38,820
Calm down.

179
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:02,940
Hello, sir.

180
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:04,940
Oh.

181
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:09,420
Here he is, Gott.

182
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,620
The man who handled the job for you.

183
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:13,980
Ah.

184
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:18,220
Hey, good work.
Clean, no one suspected a thing.

185
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:20,060
I won't ask how.

186
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:21,900
A masterwork this clean.

187
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:24,740
What do you want?

188
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:26,580
What's your name again?

189
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:27,420
Gott.

190
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,300
- Gott, sir.
- Gott, huh.

191
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,460
I have a favor to ask.

192
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,500
I intend to run for
the province candidate next term.

193
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:41,860
What?

194
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,900
Who the hell do you think you are?

195
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:47,080
Talk like that?

196
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:49,760
That position, people don't
even sell it for 20-30 million.

197
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:50,980
Do you have that much money?

198
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,980
- Sir, sir! I'm sorry!
- 200 million.

199
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:54,100
How's that?

200
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:57,780
I know all the businesses here.

201
00:14:58,980 --> 00:14:59,860
I pay every channel.

202
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:02,780
Breathing in and out
is money all the time.

203
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:06,180
A golden area like that,
of course everyone wants it.

204
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:10,580
Hey, hey! I'm not here to propose.

205
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:13,220
I'm not here to negotiate.

206
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:15,620
I'm here to say I'm going to do it.

207
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:16,540
Understand?

208
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:21,020
Who do you think you are?
Talking shit like that.

209
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:23,460
Get the fuck out of my sight!

210
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:24,940
Hey!

211
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,820
Shoot this bastard dead!

212
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:56,580
Well, since everyone has secrets
that aren't really secret...

213
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,220
Let's just show our cards and play.

214
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:02,220
Whoever's bigger, wins.

215
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:06,340
And don't bother sending people
to take care of me.

216
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,380
Because no matter who comes,
they'll die.

217
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:11,780
Just tell me.

218
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:13,900
How much do I have to pay?

219
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,060
Don't even think about it.

220
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,140
Let's just play the game.

221
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,380
Let's just play the game.

222
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:07,500
The images in my head are so clear.

223
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,300
Are you still having a headache?

224
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,060
Not anymore.

225
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:17,980
It just suddenly went away.

226
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:21,500
You seem so worried about me.

227
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:27,100
Do you like me?

228
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,940
No, I... I'm just worried.

229
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,220
Hmph.

230
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,260
So tough.

231
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:47,020
Hey.

232
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:51,220
That book you mentioned, what is it?

233
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:55,620
When you fainted, you kept repeating it
until I remembered.

234
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,020
I don't know.

235
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:03,380
I just remember that...

236
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:06,260
Why are people fighting over it so much?

237
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,980
And this book... it contains...

238
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:14,980
the elements of
Earth, Water, Wind, and Fire?

239
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,780
All within the book.

240
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:19,230
You have to find people
who possess all four elements.

241
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,740
Only then can the book be opened.

242
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:23,900
Why are you asking?

243
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:26,540
Hmm.

244
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,420
It sounds like a book my father used to
tell me about when I was a kid.

245
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:35,860
The images on the boat are scary.

246
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:37,580
I don't want to think about them.

247
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:42,660
Honestly...

248
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,500
I like how I feel right now.

249
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:47,940
Don't have to think about the past.

250
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,180
How you feel right now...

251
00:18:59,820 --> 00:19:00,780
You mean in the dark like this?

252
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:04,740
It's pitch dark here.

253
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:14,460
How could you talk to him like that?

254
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:17,460
Ugh, we're all going to get killed.

255
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,260
The plans we had are ruined! All ruined!

256
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:22,940
Why did you have to say it?

257
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:25,940
Yeah, couldn't you have waited?
We were just introducing ourselves.

258
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:28,700
A waste of time, seriously.

259
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:30,380
Can't we just be direct?

260
00:19:30,490 --> 00:19:33,300
Hinting back and forth.
He knows you, you know him.

261
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:34,940
So annoying.

262
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:39,780
What if... what if he sends an army?

263
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,980
An army of hitmen, man!

264
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:51,060
- He wouldn't dare.
- He wouldn't dare.

265
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:52,660
You're being naive.

266
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:53,820
What if he dares to?

267
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,380
I don't know. You have to help me.

268
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,820
I'm an ordinary guy.
I can get shot, you know!

269
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:01,340
Damn it.

270
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:23,220
Oh gods and spirits, please protect Singh.

271
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:29,180
Dear, if you're watching over us...

272
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:32,460
please take care of Singh, our son.

273
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:58,420
Hey, Singh.

274
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:01,180
Next week, there's a group of foreigners
chartering your boat.

275
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,620
You go pick them up.

276
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:06,100
Ten foreigners. Plenty of money.

277
00:21:07,940 --> 00:21:08,540
Oof.

278
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:11,340
Tough guy. So quiet today.

279
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:13,180
Fine, suit yourself.

280
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:16,820
Damn, not talking?
Don't ever ask me to crack jokes again.

281
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,700
I'll just pack up.

282
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:25,420
I bothered to dig up a good joke.

283
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:49,540
Matyano Matya

284
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:53,180
Matithi Sothaya Sapasa

285
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:55,980
Nomana Thenasa

286
00:22:18,330 --> 00:22:19,420
Hey, hey, hey!

287
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:20,660
Where do you think you're going?

288
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:23,620
I want to go home. I miss my mom.

289
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:24,900
Don't want to get drunk tonight.

290
00:22:25,340 --> 00:22:26,060
Huh?

291
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:28,020
You bastard,
"don't want to get drunk,"

292
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:29,660
but you're drinking beer?

293
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:32,220
Damn, this guy has gone completely crazy.

294
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:48,820
Hey, Singh.

295
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:52,420
I told you, don't be impatient, man.

296
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:54,020
Don't, you hear me?

297
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:58,300
Just tell me. Foon is still my friend, you know.

298
00:23:00,740 --> 00:23:01,540
Fine.

299
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:03,780
But you have to do something for me.

300
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:10,700
Fine, tell me.

301
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:12,620
Okay.

302
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,660
I know where Foon is.

303
00:23:17,060 --> 00:23:18,900
They're meeting to deliver the drugs and money there.

304
00:23:20,220 --> 00:23:23,340
But you have to get the money back too.

305
00:23:24,460 --> 00:23:25,340
I'm serious, you have to get it.

306
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,580
Just dump the damn drugs, let it go.

307
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:30,580
Okay.

308
00:23:32,540 --> 00:23:35,380
Foon is heavily addicted right now.

309
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:38,260
Boy's gang keeps drugging him
so he can't leave.

310
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:40,780
Stuck in there somewhere.

311
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:42,460
Boy's house, near the ice factory.

312
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:49,100
That bastard Boy.

313
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:09,860
Hey!

314
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:12,460
What the hell are these freaks?

315
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:16,060
Hey! Where's the woman named Foon?

316
00:24:16,620 --> 00:24:17,420
Where's Boy?

317
00:24:18,780 --> 00:24:21,260
You should be asking
who her husband is!

318
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:27,100
Are you messing with me, fuckerl?
Huh? Tell me, where's Foon?!

319
00:24:32,980 --> 00:24:34,180
You animal!

320
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:39,180
What's the big deal?

321
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,620
Got it, man. Let go!

322
00:24:42,220 --> 00:24:43,620
You have such a big mouth, huh?

323
00:25:00,220 --> 00:25:01,700
Hey! Hey!

324
00:25:02,340 --> 00:25:04,350
- What are you doing? Who are you?
- Jo.

325
00:25:04,380 --> 00:25:05,840
- Get this bastard out of here.
- Yeah.

326
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:12,260
These are my friends.

327
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:15,340
I think you've had enough fun.

328
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:18,940
Hey, hey!

329
00:25:19,420 --> 00:25:21,180
Singh! Singh, enough!

330
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:22,460
Leave him alone, Singh.

331
00:25:22,740 --> 00:25:24,820
- Singh!
- Your friend here is such a good fuck!

332
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:26,900
- Shut up, you animal!
- Singh.

333
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,140
Singh! Singh!

334
00:25:28,380 --> 00:25:31,500
- Singh, Singh!
- You want to get high so bad, fucker?

335
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:33,940
- Huh? You animal! Dun!
- Don't!

336
00:25:34,580 --> 00:25:35,820
Get Foon out of here.

337
00:25:37,300 --> 00:25:39,100
Toone! Toone!

338
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:41,260
- You did this to my friend, fucker?!
- Singh, don't!

339
00:25:42,180 --> 00:25:43,500
Take the money out too.

340
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:46,300
Quickly!

341
00:25:51,380 --> 00:25:53,580
Damn, run! Many of them are coming!

342
00:25:53,780 --> 00:25:54,420
Go!

343
00:26:22,420 --> 00:26:23,660
<i>Are you home yet?</i>

344
00:26:25,260 --> 00:26:26,180
I've been home for a while.

345
00:26:27,340 --> 00:26:29,060
<i>And you didn't even message me.</i>

346
00:26:29,300 --> 00:26:32,100
<i>Yeah, yeah. That's all.
We're closing up soon.</i>

347
00:26:54,900 --> 00:26:55,820
Did he talk?

348
00:26:56,380 --> 00:26:57,660
Who is the person with Anon?

349
00:26:58,820 --> 00:27:00,340
He's been telling us
for almost a month, sir.

350
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:04,020
All we know is his name is Gott.
Just "Gott."

351
00:27:05,140 --> 00:27:06,260
No address.

352
00:27:06,820 --> 00:27:08,700
And he didn't say anything else
besides that, sir.

353
00:27:09,740 --> 00:27:12,740
Damn it! I've told you everything!
I really only know this much!

354
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:16,780
You're not telling everything.
Spit it all out!

355
00:27:18,420 --> 00:27:20,380
Stop, stop! I'll talk, I'll talk!

356
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,540
He's a practitioner of dark arts.

357
00:27:22,740 --> 00:27:26,260
He's killed a lot of Anon's men.
Even Anon himself is scared of him.

358
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:28,900
He uses black magic on people.

359
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:32,100
People who die without a cause,
it's because...

360
00:27:38,540 --> 00:27:40,940
Good at lying.
Both the boss and the underlings, you.

361
00:28:00,300 --> 00:28:01,100
You bastard.

362
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:08,660
Trying me, are you?

363
00:28:09,620 --> 00:28:11,700
You have no right to know who I am.

364
00:28:13,030 --> 00:28:16,270
Cockroaches like
you are so disgusting.

365
00:28:16,290 --> 00:28:19,300
It would be fun to step on you
and watch your guts burst.

366
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:23,900
The sound must be lovely.

367
00:28:25,420 --> 00:28:27,660
You don't know why you're even alive.

368
00:28:28,340 --> 00:28:29,500
Truly worthless.

369
00:28:30,940 --> 00:28:32,060
You animal!

370
00:28:32,300 --> 00:28:33,820
What the hell are you playing at?

371
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,580
Trying me, are you?

372
00:29:13,420 --> 00:29:14,740
You challenging me?

373
00:29:33,780 --> 00:29:34,580
Hey!

374
00:30:32,780 --> 00:30:35,500
- Is there any other evidence?
- None at all, sir.

375
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:38,940
Just the lime we found on the body, sir.

376
00:30:40,220 --> 00:30:41,100
Lime?

377
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:42,380
Yes, sir.

378
00:30:56,100 --> 00:31:00,220
It's weird, man. When we found the body
in the trash bin, walking around it...

379
00:31:00,620 --> 00:31:02,620
there was lime sprinkled all over.

380
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:06,180
Soon after,
dogs started howling everywhere.

381
00:31:06,620 --> 00:31:08,620
They don't normally howl in the morning.

382
00:31:09,460 --> 00:31:11,220
Unless they see ghosts.

383
00:31:14,180 --> 00:31:15,140
Excuse me.

384
00:31:16,140 --> 00:31:17,860
Ah, running late.

385
00:31:18,650 --> 00:31:19,460
*sigh*

386
00:31:19,860 --> 00:31:21,100
I won't repeat myself.

387
00:31:21,700 --> 00:31:25,020
The body belongs to Pramuan Mingphon.

388
00:31:26,060 --> 00:31:27,900
Time of death, about six hours ago.

389
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:29,100
Mm-hmm.

390
00:31:29,420 --> 00:31:31,460
Internal organs are fine.

391
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:34,580
But he bit his own tongue clean off.

392
00:31:35,020 --> 00:31:36,580
And swallowed it.

393
00:31:37,860 --> 00:31:41,790
Normally, a human tongue
doesn't extend this long.

394
00:31:41,890 --> 00:31:42,320
Right.

395
00:31:42,500 --> 00:31:45,420
Unless something is pulling
on it or the neck is tied.

396
00:31:46,010 --> 00:31:47,180
It wouldn't come out like this.

397
00:31:47,540 --> 00:31:50,780
But in this case,
it's as if the deceased...

398
00:31:51,100 --> 00:31:54,060
had no conscious control
over his body at all.

399
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:57,300
So it could be pulled out to this length.

400
00:31:57,540 --> 00:32:00,740
Before he bit through it and bled out.

401
00:32:01,340 --> 00:32:02,060
And died.

402
00:32:02,820 --> 00:32:07,100
And what did you say?
Lime sprinkled around? Not lime.

403
00:32:07,380 --> 00:32:07,900
Ah.

404
00:32:08,620 --> 00:32:10,700
It's bone powder.

405
00:32:11,580 --> 00:32:13,300
Ashes from a human or animal.

406
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:16,300
We're sending it for analysis now.

407
00:32:22,660 --> 00:32:25,460
And there's no other source or cause?

408
00:32:26,260 --> 00:32:26,980
No.

409
00:32:27,780 --> 00:32:28,660
But what we do know is...

410
00:32:28,940 --> 00:32:30,020
before he died,

411
00:32:30,660 --> 00:32:32,340
he was definitely beaten severely.

412
00:32:33,380 --> 00:32:34,180
The condition...

413
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:39,660
Here, look.

414
00:32:43,860 --> 00:32:44,940
Hey, but there's one thing.

415
00:32:45,980 --> 00:32:47,820
- My grandfather used to tell me...
- Mm-hmm.

416
00:32:48,380 --> 00:32:51,580
A worker at our house...
got "possessed by the wind."

417
00:32:52,620 --> 00:32:53,700
Because of this thing.

418
00:32:53,750 --> 00:32:56,780
He liked to respond to
strange sounds at night.

419
00:32:57,380 --> 00:32:58,740
So something entered him.

420
00:32:59,820 --> 00:33:00,940
Once it entered,

421
00:33:01,260 --> 00:33:02,660
his voice changed.

422
00:33:03,300 --> 00:33:04,970
He talked nonsense.

423
00:33:05,120 --> 00:33:07,860
- Saw people and ran toward...
- Hey, what was that?

424
00:33:18,580 --> 00:33:19,540
My stuff fell.

425
00:33:20,620 --> 00:33:22,340
I knocked it over myself.

426
00:33:27,220 --> 00:33:28,020
Knocked it over.

427
00:33:28,100 --> 00:33:29,860
- His hand touched it.
- Mm-hmm.

428
00:33:30,700 --> 00:33:31,860
Sorry, sorry.

429
00:33:37,420 --> 00:33:39,420
The body this morning was
one of Anon's men.

430
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:41,540
Don't know where the body
was brought from.

431
00:33:43,580 --> 00:33:47,260
As for the CCTV, the signal just
happened to be lost during that time.

432
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:49,740
And it had to be lost right at that time.

433
00:33:52,460 --> 00:33:54,460
From information gathered
from the Immortal gang,

434
00:33:54,590 --> 00:33:57,340
it seems everyone knows Anon very well.

435
00:33:57,820 --> 00:33:59,780
But no one will say anything.

436
00:34:00,180 --> 00:34:02,220
Seems like there's internal conflict brewing.

437
00:34:03,660 --> 00:34:05,700
The person who could explain everything best...

438
00:34:05,860 --> 00:34:07,020
would probably be Singh.

439
00:34:18,020 --> 00:34:18,820
What should we do?

440
00:34:19,540 --> 00:34:21,460
Rachin definitely knows
we're challenging him.

441
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:24,780
He killed our man, cut out his tongue,
and stuffed him in a bin!

442
00:34:26,060 --> 00:34:27,420
Damn, we're screwed.

443
00:34:30,500 --> 00:34:31,860
Help me think, man.

444
00:34:34,380 --> 00:34:38,380
Why think we're screwed?
He should be scared of me.

445
00:34:40,140 --> 00:34:41,980
You just stay put.

446
00:34:42,660 --> 00:34:43,780
Don't do anything.

447
00:34:44,540 --> 00:34:46,660
Wait for him to come begging
and pleading on his own.

448
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:51,580
So... don't be scared at all?
Just do nothing?

449
00:34:57,230 --> 00:34:59,810
Tomorrow, they have a big shipment
delivery at the warehouse.

450
00:35:01,020 --> 00:35:02,700
If he gets that shipment, man, he's...

451
00:35:03,200 --> 00:35:04,740
He's set for life.

452
00:35:05,060 --> 00:35:06,570
But on the other hand, if we get it...

453
00:35:06,910 --> 00:35:08,220
we're set for life too.

454
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:10,760
Funding for three election terms,
and he'd be broke too.

455
00:35:14,140 --> 00:35:15,780
But he knows all our men.

456
00:35:17,060 --> 00:35:18,100
Who can we use?

457
00:35:23,500 --> 00:35:26,420
- I have something important to do.
- Not yet!

458
00:35:26,660 --> 00:35:27,800
This is important!

459
00:36:07,140 --> 00:36:07,900
Why do you stop?

460
00:36:08,900 --> 00:36:12,340
I smell something weird.
It smells so rotten, Uncle.

461
00:36:13,420 --> 00:36:16,780
- Smells like something died, Uncle.
- Just ignore it.

462
00:36:16,980 --> 00:36:17,940
Don't stop.

463
00:37:13,020 --> 00:37:18,620
Abhivadana silissa niccam vuddhapacayino

464
00:37:18,940 --> 00:37:22,260
Cattaro dhamma vaddhanti

465
00:37:22,490 --> 00:37:25,190
Ayu vanno sukham

466
00:37:25,380 --> 00:37:26,940
Balam.

467
00:37:37,820 --> 00:37:40,820
Abbot, could you please bless
Singh with holy water?

468
00:37:41,180 --> 00:37:43,260
So that bad things will leave him.

469
00:37:43,860 --> 00:37:46,060
Hopefully, it can help resolve
some of his bad karma.

470
00:37:47,420 --> 00:37:49,140
Karma is action.

471
00:37:50,020 --> 00:37:54,380
We cannot change past karma.
It's already done.

472
00:37:55,390 --> 00:37:59,180
Be mindful.
Know what is bad, don't do it again.

473
00:37:59,780 --> 00:38:02,100
You get what you do.

474
00:38:06,780 --> 00:38:08,900
So it means it can't be fixed,
right, Abbot?

475
00:38:10,100 --> 00:38:13,140
Based on the condition, as I said.

476
00:38:13,780 --> 00:38:15,960
Fix your own actions.

477
00:38:16,140 --> 00:38:19,540
Fix your thoughts.
We cannot fix yesterday.

478
00:38:20,380 --> 00:38:22,780
Make a lot of merit,
do a lot of good.

479
00:38:31,980 --> 00:38:34,180
Hey, how far along is
our union investment?

480
00:38:34,980 --> 00:38:36,500
- I don't know which round we're on.
- Yeah.

481
00:38:36,580 --> 00:38:38,860
Auntie Noi hasn't sent
her payment this round.

482
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:42,300
Really? That's bad. No customers,
and she's not paying the pool either.

483
00:38:42,980 --> 00:38:44,220
There's Auntie Kae.

484
00:38:44,450 --> 00:38:46,140
- Let's go talk to her.
- Huh? Go, go!

485
00:38:46,780 --> 00:38:48,700
Singh, wait for me here. Go, go!

486
00:38:55,780 --> 00:38:57,420
- Hello, Teacher.
- Oh, Singh.

487
00:38:58,620 --> 00:38:59,560
And your mother?

488
00:39:01,060 --> 00:39:01,660
Over there.

489
00:39:01,900 --> 00:39:04,300
- Gossiping with the aunties over there.
- Ah.

490
00:39:07,810 --> 00:39:09,110
What's wrong? You look so serious, Teacher.

491
00:39:10,910 --> 00:39:13,380
Well, these days,
fewer people come to make merit.

492
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:16,380
The economy is bad, faith is dwindling.

493
00:39:17,500 --> 00:39:18,980
Nowadays, people like to go there...

494
00:39:19,620 --> 00:39:20,940
Get deluded by those...

495
00:39:21,340 --> 00:39:24,300
spirit mediums, possessing spirits,
all these magic charms and things.

496
00:39:28,060 --> 00:39:28,740
Right now,

497
00:39:29,420 --> 00:39:31,740
bad karma isn't just
catching up to you guys.

498
00:39:32,420 --> 00:39:34,940
Bad karma is catching up to me now.

499
00:39:36,260 --> 00:39:37,700
Oh? What happened?

500
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:40,580
Hmm, it's those village headmen
and subdistrict chiefs.

501
00:39:40,740 --> 00:39:42,180
The canvassers for each candidate.

502
00:39:42,570 --> 00:39:43,780
They came to see me.

503
00:39:44,260 --> 00:39:49,100
Told me to help them.
To tell the villagers to vote for them.

504
00:39:49,250 --> 00:39:50,960
If I don't help...

505
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:53,620
It will affect the budget for
building the road to the temple.

506
00:39:54,540 --> 00:39:56,600
And being the host for
the festival ceremony,

507
00:39:56,630 --> 00:40:01,180
They claim to bring festival money in
to build a new hall, a new pavilion...

508
00:40:01,200 --> 00:40:02,140
Ugh, so many talk.

509
00:40:03,070 --> 00:40:05,550
Oh, and no one reported it?
No one protested?

510
00:40:06,060 --> 00:40:07,860
This is like being forced, Teacher.

511
00:40:08,580 --> 00:40:11,060
Mafia... they really exist everywhere.

512
00:40:12,460 --> 00:40:14,300
It's just a matter of
what form they take.

513
00:40:23,300 --> 00:40:24,580
One coffee, same as usual, Auntie.

514
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:33,100
Let's have a chat.

515
00:40:46,660 --> 00:40:47,740
These days, man...

516
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:50,340
It's not like before.

517
00:40:51,340 --> 00:40:52,380
Back then, I had no power.

518
00:40:53,420 --> 00:40:55,580
Couldn't negotiate with anyone.

519
00:40:57,180 --> 00:40:57,980
Now?

520
00:40:58,980 --> 00:41:00,300
I can negotiate with anyone.

521
00:41:00,820 --> 00:41:01,820
But it's damn hard.

522
00:41:03,340 --> 00:41:04,620
Funding is hard to find.

523
00:41:08,020 --> 00:41:09,900
That's why I came to see you today.

524
00:41:13,420 --> 00:41:15,220
Just this one job.

525
00:41:16,500 --> 00:41:17,900
The money from this one shipment...

526
00:41:18,580 --> 00:41:18,980
That's it.

527
00:41:20,700 --> 00:41:21,500
I want you to do it.

528
00:41:23,620 --> 00:41:25,140
It's because no one
knows you for this job.

529
00:41:25,700 --> 00:41:27,500
Those bastards know all my men.

530
00:41:28,900 --> 00:41:31,660
You just go create a situation
and take the goods. That's all.

531
00:41:35,020 --> 00:41:35,820
I won't do it.

532
00:41:38,700 --> 00:41:40,580
I'm not here for you to negotiate.

533
00:41:41,540 --> 00:41:42,420
I'm forcing you.

534
00:41:45,740 --> 00:41:47,940
- You can't force me, Anon.
- Oh, I can.

535
00:41:48,660 --> 00:41:49,460
I can.

536
00:42:00,700 --> 00:42:02,140
- You fuck!
- Hey, hey!

537
00:42:03,700 --> 00:42:05,700
Don't mess with my family.

538
00:42:06,660 --> 00:42:08,980
- Or I'll kill you, you animal!
- No way.

539
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:10,740
I know your weakness.

540
00:42:12,700 --> 00:42:15,700
And even if you kill me,
my men will still kill them.

541
00:42:17,100 --> 00:42:18,140
You have no choice.

542
00:42:19,140 --> 00:42:21,100
You can't run from me
for the rest of your life.

543
00:42:22,700 --> 00:42:23,660
Just do this one job.

544
00:42:24,140 --> 00:42:25,780
Then I'll leave you and
your family alone forever.

545
00:42:43,620 --> 00:42:45,060
Damn, it hurts like hell.

546
00:42:45,780 --> 00:42:47,700
He said someone put a curse on me.

547
00:42:48,100 --> 00:42:50,260
Don't know if it's true. Fucking hurts.

548
00:42:51,180 --> 00:42:51,980
Ugh!

549
00:42:54,540 --> 00:42:56,820
Go find a master or a shaman
to get this thing out of me.

550
00:43:15,300 --> 00:43:16,420
Hey, where are you going?

551
00:43:16,860 --> 00:43:17,660
You stay with me for now.

552
00:43:25,380 --> 00:43:29,060
Shouldn't you go to the doctor, Mister?
But I have to go now.

553
00:43:30,060 --> 00:43:31,780
If you go, I'll shoot.

554
00:43:34,260 --> 00:43:35,380
Damn it!

555
00:43:36,810 --> 00:43:37,460
Look.

556
00:43:37,980 --> 00:43:40,860
See how Nam eats.
Almost finished the whole platter, look!

557
00:43:41,220 --> 00:43:42,140
All by herself.

558
00:43:42,980 --> 00:43:45,390
- Eats a ton. Massive amount, every time.
- Is that all she's eating?

559
00:43:45,540 --> 00:43:47,420
I'm stuffed from both
the pizza and the drinks.

560
00:43:50,220 --> 00:43:51,340
She's truly amazing.

561
00:43:51,570 --> 00:43:53,420
Totally worth it, man.
Buy one get one free.

562
00:43:53,620 --> 00:43:54,900
- Awesome.
- Miss Nam.

563
00:43:55,140 --> 00:43:57,420
- Would you like another six platters?
- Order it now!

564
00:43:57,460 --> 00:43:58,280
Whoa!

565
00:43:58,300 --> 00:44:01,020
Just kidding. Someone small
like her shouldn't eat that much.

566
00:44:01,300 --> 00:44:02,380
Hey, Singh!

567
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,220
Come eat the pizza quickly! Hurry!

568
00:44:05,180 --> 00:44:07,300
Yeah, eat up, man!

569
00:44:07,580 --> 00:44:09,860
Before Nam eats it all.

570
00:44:11,340 --> 00:44:12,220
Just kidding.

571
00:44:14,340 --> 00:44:15,620
You're late. Where have you been?

572
00:44:20,460 --> 00:44:21,620
Should I save a slice for you?

573
00:44:22,060 --> 00:44:22,620
Hmm.

574
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:26,380
Let's eat.

575
00:44:31,020 --> 00:44:31,820
What?

576
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:33,340
Aren't you eating?

577
00:44:34,660 --> 00:44:36,900
If you don't want your share,
I'll take it.

578
00:44:37,660 --> 00:44:38,460
Hey!

579
00:44:39,740 --> 00:44:40,540
Thank you.

580
00:45:02,980 --> 00:45:04,860
You can tell me anything, you know.

581
00:45:06,340 --> 00:45:07,860
Share the good times.

582
00:45:08,700 --> 00:45:09,860
Share the bad times.

583
00:45:18,300 --> 00:45:19,100
It's nothing.

584
00:45:28,080 --> 00:45:29,530
Don't keep it to yourself.

585
00:45:30,980 --> 00:45:32,620
I can see your face is full of sorrow.

586
00:45:37,500 --> 00:45:38,300
Here.

587
00:45:39,740 --> 00:45:42,740
I can make Auntie's papaya salad recipe
for customers now.

588
00:45:43,460 --> 00:45:44,260
I think...

589
00:45:45,860 --> 00:45:47,180
my future...

590
00:45:48,020 --> 00:45:50,260
is being a papaya salad vendor
just like Auntie.

591
00:45:54,620 --> 00:45:55,340
Yeah.

592
00:45:56,540 --> 00:45:57,580
I can see it.

593
00:45:58,740 --> 00:46:00,380
Auntie will be out of a job for sure.

594
00:46:07,820 --> 00:46:08,620
Hey.

595
00:46:23,420 --> 00:46:25,100
Make sure you prepare
everything properly.

596
00:46:25,980 --> 00:46:27,820
Let Anon handle the money.

597
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:30,780
But no matter what,
don't mention my name. Understand?

598
00:46:31,240 --> 00:46:31,780
Yes, sir.

599
00:46:37,300 --> 00:46:38,420
What the hell are you looking at?

600
00:46:59,340 --> 00:47:00,860
The shaman you asked me to find, sir.

601
00:47:01,420 --> 00:47:03,260
These three are the real deal.

602
00:47:03,580 --> 00:47:05,620
This one is from Thonburi side.

603
00:47:06,140 --> 00:47:07,740
This one, Intha from Tha Nam.

604
00:47:08,740 --> 00:47:09,860
Disciplined from Din Daeng.

605
00:47:11,060 --> 00:47:11,860
Hurry.

606
00:47:12,660 --> 00:47:14,740
Just do whatever you need to do.
Just make sure they're real deal.

607
00:47:15,060 --> 00:47:16,380
I'll pay anything.

608
00:47:26,460 --> 00:47:33,020
(Chanting incantations)

609
00:47:52,460 --> 00:47:54,260
The person of the Water element...

610
00:47:55,780 --> 00:47:56,780
We have him.

611
00:48:00,100 --> 00:48:03,820
The person of the Wind element
has also revealed themselves.

612
00:48:08,750 --> 00:48:09,660
Wind.

613
00:48:10,060 --> 00:48:11,020
Water.

614
00:48:11,220 --> 00:48:12,140
Fire.

615
00:48:17,820 --> 00:48:19,740
Only the Earth element are left.
